[33mcommit 5ae7df497ee90e8bab78b4b30cc53aaccb2eca23[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 23:30:12 2026 -0600

    perf(parse): decode a whole multi-byte character without a dispatch per byte
    
    `S::run` stops at the first byte above 0x7f, so before this every CJK or emoji
    codepoint took three or four separate trips through `control` -- a
    state-machine match, a `State::Utf8` transition and a re-entry, per byte.
    `Term::utf8_share` measures those at 14.5% of btop's bytes and 28.2% of vim's.
    
    `fast_utf8` decodes one complete sequence in place. **Every unusual case
    declines and falls through to the state machine**, which is what makes it safe
    to add rather than a second implementation that can drift:
    
      * a sequence straddling the end of the read -- `read(2)` splits where it
        likes and that is what `State::Utf8` exists to carry;
      * a malformed continuation, so `[[source: unicode-ch3]]` § 3.9.5 recovery
        stays in one place;
      * any state but Ground, and any encoding but UTF-8, since under ISO 8859-1
        `single_byte` claims those bytes first.
    
    Nothing is mutated before the last thing that can decline, so a bail leaves no
    trace. The accepted path runs the same counters, the same `finish`, the same
    `Width::of` and the same `put_cp` as the `State::Utf8` arm, because two
    spellings of one operation drifting apart is a failure this repo has already
    had in `feed_avx2`.
    
    **The path counters caught their own gap.** `feed_with` now has four exits and
    `real_capture_is_mostly_escape_sequences_not_text` asserts they sum to 1.0: it
    went red immediately, with btop's `slow` down from 15% to 0.2% and the missing
    14.5% matching `utf8_share` exactly. `bytes_text` is a fourth bucket rather
    than a merge into `bytes_bulk`, which means "an ASCII run through `put_run`" --
    a different path with a different cost, and the recorded 19/66/15 splits would
    have stopped being comparable underneath it.
    
    566 tests, and all seven chunk-invariance properties at PROPTEST_CASES=20000,
    including `real_capture_is_chunk_invariant`. Throughput measured separately;
    the first attempt was contaminated by build contention and is not quoted.

