Date:   Thu Aug 27 20:58:52 2026 -0600

    Function and editing keys, and a bug the specification caught
    
    F1-F20 and Insert/Delete/PageUp/PageDown. Five more rows in
    `docs/input-coverage.md` to done, five to go.
    
    **The gaps are the substance.** F5-F12 are 15, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 23,
    24 -- 16 and 22 are skipped -- and F13-F20 are 25, 26, 28, 29, 31, 32,
    33, 34, skipping 27 and 30. A table written as "15 upward" is wrong from
    F6 on and sends a *neighbouring key* rather than nothing, which is the
    failure that is hardest to notice because something plausible arrives.
    The test reads both tables out of the pinned source and compares.
    
    **And that comparison caught a real bug.** F1-F4 were routed through
    `cursor_key`, which picks its introducer from `cursor_keys_application`
    -- so F1 came out as `CSI P` in normal mode where line 2529 says `SS3 P`
    flatly. DECCKM governs the *cursor* keys and nothing else. It would have
    been invisible against a hand-written expectation, because the
    expectation would have come from the same wrong idea as the code.
    
    Editing keys carry the same sequence in both DECCKM columns, which the
    test asserts from the table rather than assuming. Home and End stay
    PC-style from the table at 2485: line 2672's `CSI 1 ~` / `CSI 4 ~` are
    xterm's `sunKeyboard` alternative, not an addition, and sending both
    would be sending two different keys.
    
    552 tests.

