[33mcommit 6f2499a24644739246d3e69baabfdf4b0a24db90[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 19:01:10 2026 -0600

    Bound scroll blanking to what the row held
    
    `fill_row` wrote the full width whatever the row contained -- 200 cells
    to store 60 characters on the streaming payload. It now scans and writes
    only up to the last cell that differs from the blank.
    
    Compared against the *blank*, not `PackedCell::EMPTY`: the blank is
    `empty_with(self.style)`, so a row already empty still needs writing
    when a background colour is set, and comparing against EMPTY would skip
    exactly that case.
    
      cell amplification    before   after
      payload::streaming     20.7x   16.6x
      vim                    12.3x    6.8x
    
    In `OpMode::Runs` the effect is total rather than partial: text lives in
    the span table and never reaches the cells, so after the startup clear
    the row already equals the blank and nothing is written at all. Twenty
    thousand scrolled lines blank one screen.
    
    Throughput on the spans row: baseline medians 185/203/214 against
    226/214/227, higher in all three rounds, but the ranges overlap. By this
    repo's rule that is not a result, and the write reduction is the claim.
    
    **The other two candidates are not worth taking, on a measurement that
    went the wrong way.** A ceiling variant skipping blanking entirely --
    strictly less work, and in Runs mode writing the *same* zero cells as
    the scan version -- measured 142-150 against 213-229. Removing a read
    made it half as fast, with identical span amplification and an identical
    95/2/3 path split, so nothing about the workload changed. That is code
    shape rather than work, the effect this repo already records twice at
    4-5%.
    
    A high-water mark would therefore buy what the scan already buys minus a
    read the measurement says costs nothing, at sixteen write sites of
    invariant to maintain. Lazy blanking is the same bet a level up and
    would face the same evaluation problem. Both are recorded as needing an
    explanation for the anomaly first, because otherwise the next
    measurement is as likely to be measuring layout as work.
    
    545 tests.

