[33mcommit 2d04eaf1ba6636b6c5482584dcb895d6cb43da5b[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 14:33:48 2026 -0600

    Enumerate the input surface from the sources
    
    The coverage table for what baud must *send*, in the same shape
    `vt-coverage.md` uses for what it receives. Nothing is implemented yet
    beyond the mouse reports the parser already needed, so almost every row
    is `todo` -- a phase that has not started, which is not the same as work
    left half-done.
    
    It is a separate document because the input side has no single
    specification. Three layers exist and a row is meaningless without
    naming which one it belongs to: the base every terminal sends
    (`ctlseqs`), the `CSI key ; mods u` proposal that removes its
    ambiguities (`fixterms`), and kitty's progressive enhancement over that
    (`kitty-keyboard`). An application asks for the layer it can parse,
    which is the shape DECRQM already gives the output side.
    
    The key tables are **extracted, not transcribed**.
    `scripts/extract-keys.py` reads all ten out of `ctlseqs` -- 112 key rows
    -- and prints the line each was found at. A key table written from
    memory is exactly the "guessed table that would be unrecoverable and
    would look like it worked" this project refused for DEC line drawing.
    
    Writing the extractor found its own bug worth keeping: the tables are
    pipe-delimited, and splitting on runs of whitespace instead put
    `Cursor Right` in the wrong column, because it is just long enough to
    leave a single space before the bar. Four rows became three and a
    malformed one, and the count was 110 rather than 112.
    
    `the_input_key_tables_are_still_extractable` is the staleness check and
    the positive control together: if the extractor stops matching it
    reports zero tables, and zero would otherwise look exactly like
    agreement with a document nobody updated.
    
    The five modes that change what a key sends already exist on the receive
    side with an accessor and no producer -- DECCKM, DECKPAM, bracketed
    paste, mouse tracking, highlight tracking. That is the concrete reason
    input comes before the renderer: the parser work created the demand.
    
    520 tests, 44 sources, 27 citations.

