[33mcommit 6eee92f1ec373b0ac84a89a0252b771fd7a06d74[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 14:22:46 2026 -0600

    Require every public function to be called by a test
    
    Turning the unbounded half of the goal into something checkable. "Fully
    tested" cannot terminate; "every entry point has a test that calls it"
    can, and it is the question that was being answered wrongly.
    
    `Term::resize` had **no caller anywhere** -- not a test, not the
    benchmark -- because the property generator emits bytes and `resize` is
    an API call. Reaching it found three bugs, one a panic on window shrink.
    Of 48 public functions in `baud-core`, it was the shape of the only
    class this check would have flagged, and one remained: `stride`, now
    tested for the thing that makes it dangerous -- it is the row *pitch*,
    not the column count, so `viewport().len()` is `rows * stride`, and it
    stays fixed across a resize while the geometry does not.
    
    Deliberately not line coverage. Most of what this audit found was in
    code the tests already executed: `soft_reset` ran on every relevant test
    and was still wrong about the alternate screen, and both feeds executed
    the parameter loop while disagreeing past sixteen. A line percentage
    would have been high throughout and said nothing.
    
    The exemption list is empty and should stay that way. A name belongs
    there only when calling it from a test is impossible rather than
    awkward, and awkward is exactly what `resize` was.
    
    519 tests.

