[33mcommit ec4d2e0d78abd994317048b2425b529c7314f38f[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 14:13:00 2026 -0600

    Pin the input-side sources before writing any input code
    
    Input is next, so this is the same first move the parser work made:
    fetch and hash-pin the specifications before there is any code to argue
    from. Group H in the manifest, 42 sources -> 44.
    
    The output side has one specification to enumerate against. The input
    side does not: what exists is a base every terminal implements and two
    layered proposals to escape its ambiguities.
    
    - `ctlseqs` already carries the base -- "PC-Style Function Keys",
      `modifyOtherKeys`, and the cursor and keypad application modes -- so it
      is group C *and* group H rather than being fetched twice.
    - `fixterms` is where `CSI unicode-key ; modifiers u` comes from. Pinned
      separately from kitty's protocol on purpose: kitty extends it, so a
      claim about "CSI u" has to name which of the two it means.
    - `kitty-keyboard` is the progressive-enhancement protocol, `CSI > flags
      u` to push and `CSI < u` to pop. Worth having because it is the only
      input specification that enumerates its own escape hatch -- an
      application asks for exactly the enhancements it can parse -- which is
      the shape the output side already uses for DECRQM.
    
    Both were verified rather than assumed. A raw grep for `CSI 27` and
    `CSI > 1 u` missed in both files; stripping markup finds them, along
    with `CSIu`, `1;5u` and `progressiveenhancement`. That is the same trap
    the ECMA-48 note records, and the reason the manifest comments say which
    probes fired.
    
    The checker was verified too, not trusted: appending one byte to
    `fixterms.html` makes `check-sources.sh` print FAIL *and* exit 1, and
    the clean tree exits 0. A gate that prints without failing is the
    `inf x amplification` shape.
    
    Known debt, unchanged by this: the manifest declares note groups A-H and
    only B exists under docs/research/notes/. H needs one before anything
    cites it for a design decision rather than a fact.

