[33mcommit 657e1cbdcb8f1995f1f465943fc50717c1b3c523[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 14:01:56 2026 -0600

    Add Term::get_row, the checked half of the pair
    
    `row` takes its index on trust and does not fail loudly when that trust
    is misplaced: the buffer is `MAX_ROWS` deep and the grid is `rows` deep,
    so an index between them is allocated memory that is not on screen and
    comes back looking like cells.
    
    `get_row` is the `slice::get` to its `slice[i]`. Purely additive --
    `row`'s behaviour is unchanged and nothing published moves -- so a
    caller that cannot prove its index is in range now has something to call
    that is not silently wrong.
    
    The case it exists for is not hypothetical. An embedder holding a row
    count across a resize is the same staleness that turned a shrink into a
    panic in `viewport` and an out-of-grid cursor in DECRC, both fixed
    earlier today.
    
    Zero performance question attached: `row` has no callers on the ingest
    path -- `parse/`, `text.rs` and `scan/` contain none -- so neither it nor
    this touches any measured number. The two invariants are about the bytes
    per input byte and the working set of the ingest loop; this is a
    renderer-facing accessor read once per row per frame.
    
    Making `row` itself panic or return `Option` remains open, and is a
    deliberate change to a published signature rather than one to slip into
    a testing pass.
    
    517 tests.

