[33mcommit 2e6124b542791198fb2ad93dc7748f5fd81cba3e[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 13:52:06 2026 -0600

    Pin Term::row's out-of-grid behaviour and document the precondition
    
    Auditing the public API for the same class as the resize bugs -- entry
    points the byte-driven generator cannot reach -- leaves two that take a
    position. `marks` is safe by construction: it hashes into a fixed table
    and `is_for` rejects a slot that is not the cell asked for, so an
    out-of-range coordinate yields an empty iterator.
    
    `row` is not. The buffer is `MAX_ROWS` deep and the grid is `rows` deep,
    so an index between them is allocated memory that is not part of the
    screen: `row(55)` on a fifty-row screen returns real cells from physical
    row 55. No panic and no `None` -- silently the wrong data, which is the
    shape this project rules out for replies.
    
    Pinned and documented rather than changed. Answering honestly means
    returning `Option` or panicking, and both alter a published signature or
    its behaviour; that is a decision to take deliberately, not one to slip
    into a testing pass. `viewport` is the bounded accessor and has no such
    edge, and it is what the benchmarks and tests use.
    
    516 tests.

