    Generate SOS/PM/APC control strings, and fix the roadmap
    
    The DCS family was the one introducer neither reach check covered, and
    the gap was not where I expected. DECRQSS settings are complete: the
    generator asks for all five baud answers plus two it must refuse.
    
    What had no coverage at all was `sos_pm_apc_string` -- SOS, PM, APC and
    non-DECRQSS DCS. That family matters more than the arity of any single
    operation, because its failure mode is not "an operation is missing" but
    "the payload was executed as commands", which is the bug this parser
    already had when those states fell through to Ground.
    `apc_payload_is_not_executed` pins one case; nothing generated any.
    
    `Op::ControlString` emits all four introducers over six payloads: four
    with no `ESC`, which must be consumed in silence, and two containing one,
    which legitimately *cancel* the string per williams and run what follows
    -- worth generating precisely because both feeds have to agree on where
    the cancel happened. Terminated with the 7-bit `ESC \` only: `9C` is ST's
    8-bit spelling but is a continuation byte under UTF-8 and correctly does
    not terminate, so generating it would swallow the rest of the program.
    
    51 properties green at PROPTEST_CASES=20000. Nothing broke, which is a
    weaker result than a bug and still the point: the family is exercised
    rather than assumed.
    
    The roadmap is corrected to match the owner's: input is next, then the
    renderer. This file said shaping first, which disagreed with the repo
    description. Item 3 also dropped "the missing 56 operations" -- this
    file's own Unmeasured section records that as closed.

