[33mcommit 8aa593010bfef44b7e3136277e00c2372d77cad0[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 11:27:24 2026 -0600

    Enumerate ESC and OSC generator reach, not just CSI
    
    The CSI reach check left ESC, OSC and DCS unenumerated, which was the
    honest remaining gap. This closes it the same way: read
    `docs/vt-coverage.md`, draw a corpus from the strategy the properties
    use, and require every `done` row to appear.
    
    The ESC pass found nine unreachable -- DECKPAM, DECKPNM, HTS, RIS,
    S7C1T, S8C1T, DECALN, and the two `ESC %` encoding selectors. OSC was
    already complete. DCS has nothing to enumerate: Sixel and DECUDK are
    both `out`, and DECRQSS is reached through `Op::Decrqss`.
    
    Adding the nine broke two properties, and neither was a bug in baud:
    
    - `replies_are_well_formed` asserted every reply begins with `ESC`. After
      `S8C1T` baud answers with the 8-bit C1 introducers -- `9b 3f 36 63` for
      the DA -- which is exactly what that row claims. The property was about
      the *default encoding* while wearing the name of a property about
      replies, and only passed because nothing generated could switch. It now
      accepts `9B`/`90`/`9D` and the `9C` terminator.
    - `the_alt_screen_never_leaks_into_the_primary` had to learn that RIS
      leaving the alt screen is licensed. That is the same action DECSTR was
      taking *without* the licence, which this property caught last commit,
      so the filter names RIS specifically rather than "any reset".
    
    Both checks are verified to fail: removing `Op::Hts` reports `ESC H` by
    name.
    
    505 tests, 50 properties green at PROPTEST_CASES=20000.

