[33mcommit d5c62cfd276ffb74809bf3a146317b6351568133[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 10:50:38 2026 -0600

    Widen the property generator to the shapes it could not reach
    
    The parameter-overflow bug was not found by the property suite, and
    raising the case count would never have found it: `Op::Sgr` emits
    exactly one parameter, so no generated program ever carried a long
    list. `generated_programs_are_chunk_invariant` was true of everything it
    could build. That is a different failure from too few cases, and it
    generalises -- so this closes the other axes the generator could not
    reach.
    
    - **Every SGR parameter above 107.** The table stopped there, so nothing
      generated ever set fraktur, proportional, framed, encircled,
      overlined or an ideogram aspect, and nothing exercised 23, 54 or 65 --
      the parameters that clear two, two and five bits at once. Those were
      implemented and then tested only by hand-written cases.
    - **Lists with holes** (`CSI 1;;4 m`), where an omitted parameter means
      its default. The whole `params[i] = None` path was reachable only from
      hand-written cases.
    - **Values past `Param`'s `u16`**, so the saturation in `push` is
      actually taken. The largest value the generator could previously build
      was three digits, so a wrapping implementation would have passed
      every property here.
    - **C0 controls spliced inside a sequence**, which williams executes
      while the sequence continues.
    
    `the_generator_reaches_the_shapes_it_claims` asserts each new op emits
    the bytes it claims. An op that silently emits the wrong thing is
    indistinguishable from one whose shape is never buggy -- the same
    failure as a search probe that cannot match.
    
    No new bugs surfaced: 47 properties green at PROPTEST_CASES=20000 with
    all four axes reachable. 499 tests.

