    Cover the DCS parameter path and guard the capacity cast
    
    Two gaps left by the previous three commits.
    
    `dcs_param_byte` got the same bound as `csi_param_byte` and had no test
    for it -- every overflow case drove `CSI`, and the DECRQSS tests send no
    numeric parameters at all. "The fix is symmetric so it must be fine" is
    the reasoning that let `machine.rs` diverge from `fast.rs` to begin
    with. Verified the same way as the CSI case: with the bound removed the
    test fails, and it fails by *panicking* on an out-of-range index, since
    `next_capped` now lets the position reach `CAPACITY`. No shipped version
    could reach that -- the old code pinned at capacity and corrupted
    instead -- but the check is load-bearing rather than tidy.
    
    `ParamIdx::PAST_LAST` casts the capacity into a `u8` unguarded, while
    `SubParams` asserts against `u64::BITS`. `Attrs` has fourteen free bits,
    so `WIRE` can still grow and take `CAPACITY` with it; the parallel
    assert means neither constant can drift alone.
    
    498 tests.

