[33mcommit d80ed1f543f000442172bc064cf830d5604818ca[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 08:19:21 2026 -0600

    Size the parameter array from what DECRQSS has to re-read
    
    baud emitted a DECRQSS reply baud could not parse. DECRQSS answers with
    something the application can send back verbatim, so a reply the parser
    cannot re-read is a reply that does not round-trip -- and at 16
    parameters it could not.
    
    The minimum reachable case is not exotic: bold with a foreground, a
    background and an underline colour goes in as sixteen parameters and
    comes back as seventeen (`0;1;58;2;..;38;2;..;48;2;..`). That is an
    editor drawing an undercurl over truecolour text. The maximal case, all
    eighteen attributes plus a font and three colours, is 35. The reply
    buffer was never the problem -- that reply is 109 bytes against
    `REPLY` = 256.
    
    `ParamIdx::CAPACITY` is now `1 + Attrs::WIRE.len() + 1 + 3 * 5`, derived
    rather than chosen, so it cannot go back out of step the next time
    `WIRE` grows -- which is how it drifted: `WIRE` went 13 -> 18 with the
    ideogram aspects and nothing said the limit had moved. `SubParams`
    widens to `u64` to keep one bit per parameter, with a `const` assert
    tying the two.
    
    Both round-trips are pinned, at seventeen parameters and at the
    maximum, and the overflow tests are now capacity-relative rather than
    spelling `16`.
    
    A/B on Host B, medians of 9 interleaved: spans 195.0 -> 198.9, promote
    hybrid 219.3 -> 219.5, TUI through a PTY 215.9 -> 220.5. Every range
    overlaps, so there is no result. Recorded with the caveat that both
    payloads send short parameter lists, so this measures `Term` growing
    ~82 bytes and not the deeper array being walked.
    
    Also records a finding found on the way and not acted on: `StyleWord::
    key` omits `underline` and `font` while claiming to fold "everything
    that distinguishes one rendition from another". It is a hit-rate cost,
    not a correctness bug -- `intern_style` compares the whole word on a hit
    -- and it is unmeasurable with payloads that intern nothing, so the doc
    comment now says what it does instead of what it does not.
    
    497 tests.

