    Record the measurement and the lesson behind SGR 60-65
    
    The A/B: two binaries from the two commits, run alternating so an
    ordering effect cannot be read as a result. Ranges overlap completely on
    both rows, so there is no result -- the ideogram aspects cost nothing
    this benchmark can see.
    
    The limitation is recorded with it, because it matters more than the
    number: both payloads report `styles 0 interned / 208954 hits (100.0%)`,
    one rendition for the whole run. `StyleWord` grew 16 -> 20 bytes and the
    style table 1024 -> 1280, and a payload that interns nothing exercises
    neither. That is the "payloads that don't exercise the case" trap, and
    it is stated rather than worked around: the table measures code layout,
    not the style table.
    
    `CLAUDE.md` gains the general rule, which is the part worth keeping: a
    source you cannot search is not a source you have read, run a positive
    control before believing a MISS, and two reasons for one refusal means
    neither was checked.

