[33mcommit cf152c33eac5c65ea50d85c9861b94249ed07d48[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 07:31:32 2026 -0600

    Implement SGR 60-65; the source was readable all along
    
    `docs/vt-coverage.md` refused the ideogram aspects with "no readable
    primary source ... a scanned PDF whose text extracts letter-spaced and
    unsearchable". The PDF is not scanned. The text layer is intact and
    extracts letter-spaced -- "Operat i ng sy st em" -- which defeats exact
    phrase search and nothing else. Six probes for `framed`, `encircled`,
    `ideogram` and the rest missed because they could not have matched
    `f r amed`, and the misses were read as absence.
    
    Stripping non-alphanumerics from both sides finds every term. ECMA-48
    § 8.3.117 then defines all six parameters unambiguously: 60-64 are
    ideogram underline, double underline, overline, double overline and
    stress marking, and 65 cancels the five together.
    
    The reason this stood so long is that the refusal carried two different
    reasons that were never reconciled: the table said "no readable source"
    while `Attrs::_FREE_BITS` said they were out "because nothing sends
    them". Two reasons for one refusal is the signal that neither was
    checked.
    
    - `Attrs` u16 -> u32 for the five bits; `StyleWord` 16 -> 20 bytes with
      explicit `_pad`, since zerocopy rejects implicit padding. That is
      `NSTYLE * 4` = 256 bytes in a 24 MB `Storage` and nothing on the cell,
      which holds a `StyleId` index rather than a rendition.
    - `scripts/extract-ecma48.py` makes the extraction reproducible and
      carries a positive control, because a probe that cannot fire looks
      exactly like a fact. Its own first version had the bug in miniature:
      the offset index used `isalnum()` while the search used `[^a-z0-9]`,
      so every window landed in the wrong section.
    - 56/57 stay out with a better citation: § 8.3.117 reserves 56-59, and
      58/59 are done only because ctlseqs assigns them the underline colour,
      which is an extension over ECMA-48 rather than a reading of it.
    - 26 is a reservation ("for proportional spacing as specified in CCITT
      Recommendation T.61"), so baud records the bit and resolves nothing.
    - Corrects stale sizes in `StyleWord`, `FontId` and `tests/sgr/fonts.rs`
      that still said twelve bytes, and a `SGR 59` comment that had drifted
      onto the `26` arm.
    
    Also folds in whole-tree `treefmt` output: single-line `if/else`
    collapsing in `grid.rs`, `mode.rs`, `avx2.rs` and three others. Cosmetic
    only -- `_mm256` occurrences in `avx2.rs` unchanged at 23.
    
    147 done rows, 0 unfinished, 491 tests.

