[33mcommit f6a8a3f9b496bee8d1343059e79a23a6e54f250e[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 06:41:47 2026 -0600

    The line-drawing table is complete; the gated source is not what supplied it
    
    I described a gap as "DEC line-drawing beyond what foot supplies". There is
    no beyond. The set differs from ASCII only in `0x60..0x7E`, which is 31
    entries, which is the whole table.
    
    The confusion has a real source in the repo rather than only in my
    phrasing: `MANIFEST.toml` still records `dec-special-graphics` as `gated`,
    with nothing next to it saying where the mapping actually came from. `gated`
    is accurate about *provenance* -- the DEC-authored table was never obtained
    in machine-readable form, and the page really is images -- and reads as a
    missing capability. It is not: `[[source: foot-vt100-0]]` carries the
    mapping, cited as foot's judgement rather than as DEC's.
    
    The entry says that now, and `the_line_drawing_table_covers_the_whole_set`
    walks every byte of the range so the claim is asserted rather than counted
    by hand -- and checks that nothing outside it is touched, since "translates
    under the graphics set" would be just as wrong applied to `A`.

