[33mcommit 87a421e1b7338e1663f173bc48af7deb984b9ec7[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 06:34:34 2026 -0600

    SGR 60-65: the reason is no readable source, not the bit budget
    
    I wrote that these cost widening `Attrs` to `u32` -- 256 bytes -- and that
    nothing sends them. Both true, and neither is the binding constraint. I went
    to implement them and could not find out what they mean.
    
    `[[source: ctlseqs]]`'s SGR section stops before 60. `[[source: ecma48]]` is
    a scanned PDF: the streams inflate, but the text is drawn with per-glyph
    positioning, so extraction gives letter-spaced fragments -- "Operat i ng sy
    st em" -- and phrase search fails. Every quote this repo already takes from
    it was transcribed by eye from the rendered page.
    
    So implementing them means writing a control function from memory, which is
    the one thing CLAUDE.md forbids outright, and with reason: the spec has
    overruled confident guesses here repeatedly.
    
    The row says that now, and says explicitly that bits are *not* the obstacle
    -- three are free and widening is 256 bytes -- so nobody re-derives a budget
    argument that was never what stopped it. MANIFEST.toml records the
    extraction finding next to the source, the same way it records that the DEC
    line-drawing table is images.

