[33mcommit bfc34af2b6aba1f183de9b4638407ceb072f7c71[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 06:26:41 2026 -0600

    SGR presentation attributes: Fraktur, proportional, framed, overlined
    
    Same reason as fonts -- "no renderer consumes them" -- and it resolves the
    same way. These are renditions, `Attrs` had eight free bits, and
    `Term::style_of` is where a renderer reads one.
    
    Two parameters clear two attributes each, which is the part worth getting
    right: `[[source: ecma48]]` § 8.3.117 names `SGR 23` "not italicized, not
    fraktur", and `SGR 54` clears framed and encircled together. Clearing one of
    each pair would leave the other set with no parameter that turns it off --
    a rendition an application could enter and not leave.
    
    `Attrs::WIRE` is a table rather than a match precisely so DECRQSS cannot
    forget a new attribute, and it did not: adding five entries reported five.
    That is the shape that stopped `fold` discarding everything except reset and
    foreground.
    
    `60-65` stay out and the reason is now *measured* rather than asserted: five
    bits are needed and three are free, so they cost widening `Attrs` to `u32`
    -- `NSTYLE * 4` bytes, 256 in a 24 MB Storage. Nothing sends them, which is
    the scope decision; the structure is not the obstacle, and saying it was
    would be the mistake that kept fonts and the underline colour out. `56` and
    `57` are out because ctlseqs assigns them nothing at all.

