[33mcommit 234e99bd5fbc7f1a715bae7c9f587a96a6da55d8[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 01:54:39 2026 -0600

    Stop discarding combining marks
    
    `put_cp` returned early on `Width::ZERO`, so every combining mark was
    silently thrown away: `e` + U+0301 stored `e` and the accent was **gone** --
    not mis-measured, absent, and unrecoverable by a renderer, a selection or a
    copy. A terminal must not lose a character it was sent. This predates the
    width work; the generated tables only made it reachable for more scripts.
    
    Marks are stored against the cell they attach to, in a table beside the grid
    rather than in it. `PackedCell` is eight measured bytes and `CellFlags` is
    fully allocated -- two bits of flags, fourteen of LinkId -- so there is no
    room in the cell, and a ninth byte would round it to twelve.
    
    Bounded and evicting on collision, for the reason NLINK and NSTYLE are: the
    key is attacker-supplied, since a page can emit as many marks as it likes,
    and a growable table under that pressure is the content-addressing failure
    mode CLAUDE.md already refuses. A cell that loses its slot keeps its base
    character. marks_dropped and marks_evicted keep the bound visible; a mark
    with no base is dropped and counted, because GB1 makes a leading mark its
    own cluster and there is no cell for it.
    
    The audit refused the first version -- 8 new casts against a budget of 8,
    and that budget is a floor, not slack. Fixed the way the CLAUDE.md table
    describes rather than by raising it: MarkSlot::{index_of, for_cell, is_for,
    push, CAPACITY} now own the arithmetic, so the casts live in baud-domain
    where a newtype's job is to wrap a primitive. index_of takes Row and Col
    rather than two integers, because passing them the wrong way round compiles
    and gives a plausible index into the wrong slot.
    
    **Measured faster, and that is the finding.** 999.3 [988.1-1006.9] and
    992.1 [983.4-1003.2] before, against 1043.6 [1029.6-1054.9] and 1038.3
    [1020.7-1044.5] after, ghostty stable, ranges not overlapping in either
    pair. It roughly cancels the width regression -- and two changes that an
    ASCII payload never executes moving throughput 5% down and 4.5% back up is
    the strongest evidence yet that both numbers are code and data layout, not
    work. Recorded in CLAUDE.md: resolve it with a linker map or perf on the
    ingest loop if it is ever worth resolving, not by reverting features.
    
    Full cluster semantics -- a ZWJ sequence occupying one cell rather than four
    columns -- is still out, and now for a stated reason rather than an
    unmeasured one: it needs the cell to know its cluster and CellFlags has no
    free bits.
    
    Done count 125 -> 126.

