Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Thu Aug 27 01:07:33 2026 -0600

    Enumerate grapheme clustering as a scope decision; plainer description
    
    Two loose ends, both about not claiming more than is true.
    
    Grapheme clustering existed only in a research note, which meant the one
    genuinely large gap on the protocol surface was not in the enumerated table
    that is supposed to be the scope definition. It has rows now, as `out` with
    the reason, alongside the width work that is done.
    
    The consequence is stated as arithmetic rather than as a caveat: `U+1F469
    U+200D U+1F4BB` is one cluster and one glyph, and baud gives it **four**
    columns, because both emoji are East Asian Wide and the joiner is zero. It
    stays out because the cost is unmeasured, not because it is unwanted --
    PackedCell is eight measured bytes and a cluster needs storage the cell does
    not have, so it means a side table whose cost against the working-set rule
    nobody here has measured. Note G § 4.4 and § 4.5 carry the detail and the
    reason there is no consensus to conform to yet.
    
    What matters is that nothing claims it. DECRQM `?2027` answers 0, not
    recognized -- not 2, which would tell an application the mode exists and is
    merely off, whereupon it would set it and believe it took effect. Pinned by
    decrqm_does_not_claim_grapheme_clustering, and the row becomes 3 when
    clustering lands.
    
    Description is now "A terminal emulator written in Rust, under
    construction." The previous one still carried a status claim in a second
    sentence, which was the "too detailed" half of the objection; the ego half
    went earlier with the comparative framing. README and Cargo.toml match.
    
    Done count 123 -> 124.

