    implementations named rather than smoothed into a false consensus.
    
    I re-fetched and re-hashed every source by hand before pinning. The four
    sha256 values it reported -- unicode-ch3, uax11, uax29, ecma35 -- each
    reproduced byte-for-byte, as did iso10646-fcd's. That is why the note's
    citations are trusted enough to act on rather than merely read.
    
    Six sources pinned, group G declared. iso10646-fcd is recorded as the Final
    Committee Draft it is, with the clause renumbering to the published edition
    written into the manifest comment (11 -> 12, 12.2 -> 13.2, 12.5 -> 13.5), so
    a reader checking a citation against published ISO text is not surprised.
    
