[33mcommit 721bfe5dad99ef3a699dfb2b4626f769ce6c2aad[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 22:10:06 2026 -0600

    docs: the private modes were implemented and never documented or tested
    
    You were right that the docs did not get updated. Three concrete gaps:
    
    * **`vt-coverage.md` had no rows for the nine private modes** added in the
      previous commit — DECCKM, DECANM, DECCOLM, DECSCLM, DECSCNM, DECARM,
      cursor blink, reverse wrap, legacy `?47` and meta. One row each now,
      with what "done" means for each: for the input-side and renderer-side
      ones it means an accessor an embedder can read, which is the only
      channel a core with no keyboard and no renderer has.
    
    * **Four of them had no behavioural test.** `coverage.rs` said so the
      moment the rows existed, naming `?1`, `?3`, `?5` and `?8` — the check
      working. `tests/vt100/private_modes.rs` covers all nine: default-off
      and toggling, that they do not alias each other (they share a `u16`
      bitset now at 15 of 16 bits), that DECCOLM clears and homes but does
      **not** resize because geometry is caller-owned, that `?12` changes
      blink without changing the cursor *shape*, that `?47` does not save the
      cursor where `?1049` does, and that a multi-parameter form applies to
      every parameter.
    
    * **Every quoted count was stale.** README, CLAUDE.md and MEASUREMENTS.md
      all said "92 rows at done" against a table with 110, and README said
      "321 tests" against 364.
    
    The last one is the interesting failure, because I had already written a
    test to stop exactly this class of thing and then let a different
    instance of it rot. So the fix is a gate, not a correction:
    `coverage.rs::quoted_counts_match_reality` parses the table and fails if
    any prose count disagrees. It named all three files on its first run.
    
    README's test count is deleted rather than corrected. A number that
    changes with every commit and is quoted in prose can only ever rot; the
    command to run the suite is what a reader actually needs.

