[33mcommit 7658d74d8b6e1a930873c12b718d8e38facd4768[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 20:47:30 2026 -0600

    docs: make every documented claim either checked or deleted
    
    The docs had drifted badly and, worse, claimed enforcement they did not
    have. Three audits found 14 wrong facts, 4 self-contradictions and 5
    broken paths.
    
    **The sharpest one, fixed properly.** `docs/vt-coverage.md` said it was
    "checked by `tests/coverage.rs`: every row marked done must have a named
    test ... A row cannot be marked done without one." **That file did not
    exist.** The document whose stated purpose is preventing "documentation
    that claims coverage it does not have" was doing exactly that, in the
    paragraph where it said so.
    
    `baud-core/tests/coverage.rs` now exists and gates CI. It is honest about
    its limits: it proves every `done` row is mentioned by some test, and it
    *cannot* prove the test would fail on a regression — nothing mechanical
    can. The document now says that in those words instead of implying a
    guarantee. A weaker check that is real beats a stronger claim that is
    not. Verified by inventing a `done` row and watching it fail.
    
    **The README's example is now compiled.** It had none at all, despite
    crates.io and docs.rs badges — a reader arriving from either could not
    find out how to call the library. It is
    `baud-core/examples/quickstart.rs`, built by `cargo check --all-targets`,
    with `tests/readme.rs` asserting the README shows that file rather than a
    drifted paraphrase.
    
    **README: 354 lines -> 173.** It was 45% measurement narrative and
    protocol status, both restating files that already existed. What is left
    is a front door: status, quickstart, the two invariants, one number,
    layout, and where to read more.
    
    **New:** `docs/README.md` (the index whose absence is why README grew),
    `docs/architecture.md` (the data path, and the design rationale that was
    trapped in the agent-facing CLAUDE.md), `docs/protocol-decisions.md`
    (the 180-line design essay split out of vt-coverage.md, where nobody
    scanning a status table would ever reach it), and
    `docs/research/notes/c-vt-parser.md` — cited by vt-coverage.md as the
    sole justification for baud's one deliberate divergence from Williams'
    13-state machine, and missing.
    
    **Numbers now carry provenance.** MEASUREMENTS.md had three mutually
    incompatible ghostty verdicts with nothing saying which was current, and
    no table anywhere carried a date or commit. There is now a Host D section
    measured against this code, and Hosts A/B/C are each marked superseded
    with what they predate. Host A has never been re-run under interleaved
    ordering, which biased baud by 16-20% — that is now stated where its
    numbers are, not 300 lines away.
    
    The current result, stated honestly: in span storage baud is 1.47x
    ghostty streaming and 1.91x on TUI. In **cell** storage it is 0.96x and
    0.94x — ghostty is faster, and the README says so next to the headline
    rather than quoting only the flattering mode.
    
    Also fixed: `Storage::boxed()` described as "~1.7 MB" when it is ~24 MB;
    "~22 VT operations against alacritty's 66" still in the file a sceptic
    checks; "17 tests" when there are 321; README claiming the operation gap
    closed and then listing closed operations as not done; OSC 8 shipped and
    simultaneously listed as missing; four wrong paths; and SECURITY.md,
    which still carried its template placeholder and called baud "a Rust CLI
    project" while the repo had a real threat model written up elsewhere.

