[33mcommit 2d23dc88dbd7df249dace82d03f073a0becf7f0d[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 20:37:49 2026 -0600

    ci: run the full check suite on pre-push
    
    Local `dev-ci` green is not evidence CI is green, and relying on
    remembering to run it did not work — master sat red while the local gate
    passed, because the failure was in a job the local gate does not have.
    
    Pre-push rather than pre-commit: the thing being protected is the remote,
    not the reflog, and running the whole suite on every commit of a stack
    would make stacking unusable. `git push --no-verify` skips it on
    purpose; a gate with no escape hatch gets disabled wholesale instead.

