[33mcommit 2639a9c31c6d3d0209a0844a75b67ecc904aa717[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 20:37:03 2026 -0600

    fix: IRM was recorded and reported but never acted on
    
    `ModeBit::InsertReplace` was set by SM/RM and answered by DECRQM, and
    nothing in the write path read it. An application sent `CSI 4 h`, wrote
    text expecting insertion, got overwrite — and DECRQM confirmed the mode
    was on, so it had no way to find out.
    
    That is two of the three rules `docs/vt-coverage.md` calls
    non-negotiable, broken at once: *never record a mode you do not act on*,
    and *never answer a query with the wrong shape*. It was visible in the
    coverage table as `partial` while README claimed "every Tier 1
    VT100/ANSI operation".
    
    `[[source: ecma48]]` 8.3.64: with IRM set the graphic character is
    inserted and the line from the cursor moves right. Implemented in both
    write paths — `put_run` for bulk ASCII, `put_cp` for decoded codepoints —
    bounded by the right margin, opening two cells for a double-width
    character. `OpMode::Runs` promotes first: a run records "these bytes at
    this position", so shifting the tail invalidates every run after the
    cursor.
    
    **The first implementation cost 9% of the cells path and the second
    does not.** Calling `View::insert_cells` directly from `put_run` — which
    is `#[inline(always)]` and is the measured ingest loop — inlined a large
    function into the hot loop:
    
      cells, computed   baseline 1072.6 [1039.7-1083.3]
                        naive     963.6 [ 933.1- 988.0]   <- no overlap
                        cold      1043.5 [1017.4-1054.9]  <- overlaps baseline
    
    ghostty was stable across all three runs (1086.2 / 1095.9 / 1089.8), so
    that is not machine drift. The fix is `#[inline(never)]` on an
    `open_gap` helper: insert mode is rare, so it costs one predictable
    branch per run and nothing else. I nearly accepted the first pair of
    measurements, where the ranges overlapped by 15 MB/s; the second pair is
    what showed it.
    
    13 tests, all failing on the previous commit. `vt-coverage.md` moves
    `CSI h`/`CSI l` from `partial` to `done`.

