[33mcommit 86666ae7a33d69e3e22d9098989989eead06304b[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 20:19:21 2026 -0600

    refactor(core): split lib.rs into modules by responsibility
    
    `baud-core/src/lib.rs` was 2,965 lines, of which ~2,400 were a single
    `impl<'a> Term<'a>` block holding 103 methods. It is now 22 modules, the
    largest 475 lines. Pure move: no behaviour change, no signature change
    beyond visibility.
    
    `Term`'s fields stay in one struct in `term.rs` and become `pub(crate)`;
    every other module adds its own `impl Term` block. That keeps the
    measured invariant CLAUDE.md records — all state behind `&mut self`,
    because the C prototype's file-scope globals ran 16-34% slower — while
    letting each protocol area live under its own name:
    
      term storage text cursor scroll margins erase tabs style modes
      reply osc dcs charset mouse reset
      parse/{state,machine,fast}  scan/{mod,portable,avx2}
    
    Every `_mm256` now lives in `scan/avx2.rs` and nowhere else, which is the
    first thing to check after any port here.
    
    Two things the gates caught that a green host build would not have:
    
    * **The bare-metal gate caught a broken re-export.** `pub(crate) use
      avx2::*` is unconditional but everything in `avx2.rs` is
      `#[cfg(target_arch = "x86_64")]`, so on aarch64 it resolves to nothing
      and compiles fine. `x86_64-unknown-none` is where it fails. The
      re-export is now gated to match the definitions.
    * **`audit_all.sh` had to stop naming `lib.rs`.** It now walks
      `baud-core/src` and sums, printing a per-file line so it is visibly
      covering the modules. Pinned to a path it would have measured a
      60-line file of `mod`/`pub use` and reported green for ever.
    
    Verified as a pure move, same session, medians of 9:
    
      tests    306 before, 306 after -- exactly
      _mm256   23 lines before, 23 after
      cells    before 1089.9 [1063.9-1104.6]  after 1088.5 [1071.8-1102.4]
      cells TUI before  970.3 [ 944.9- 997.7]  after  983.6 [ 954.4-1022.1]
      spans    before 1653.2 [1188.3-1685.8]  after 1675.3 [1493.1-1720.9]
    
    Every range overlaps. A module boundary is not a codegen boundary under
    LTO, and the numbers say so.

