Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 20:09:22 2026 -0600

    refactor(domain): split lib.rs into modules by responsibility
    
    `baud-domain/src/lib.rs` was 4,605 lines. It is now 24 modules, the
    largest of which is 522. Nothing moved crates and nothing changed
    behaviour — this is a pure move.
    
    The seams were already documented: the file carried 18 section banners
    (`// ═══ Quantities`, `// ═══ VT operations`, …) that were doing a
    module's job in comments. Those become directories:
    
      brand pos quantity layout width style cell store line font
      decode grid source scan unchecked
      vt/{csi,esc,osc,dcs,sgr,mode,report,mouse,charset}
    
    The one thing a line-range split could not do, and the reason this was
    worth doing carefully: **impl blocks were scattered**. `Col` had impls at
    four separate points in the file (829, 1998, 3752, 4220), `StreamByte` at
    three, `Count`, `Run`, `ByteLen`, `Param`, `SgrAttr` and a dozen others
    at two or more. Each type is now in one place with all of its impls,
    which is the actual SRP win — the banners alone would not have got there.
    
    Visibility: newtype tuple fields and a handful of helpers become
    `pub(crate)`. That is exactly the scope they already had — everything in
    a single file is reachable from everywhere else in it — so no invariant
    is weakened. The opaque-newtype guarantee against *callers* is unchanged,
    because it was always `pub`-level.
    
    `audit_all.sh`'s bool gate now globs `baud-domain/src/` instead of naming
    `lib.rs`. After this split lib.rs is 40 lines of `mod`/`pub use`, so a
    path-pinned grep would have reported zero for ever — the
    "instrumentation outlived what fed it" failure CLAUDE.md records, and it
    would have happened in this commit.
    
    Verified as a pure move:
