[33mcommit 676afbf77a9030f52eb0ff86454ea777471d3918[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 19:36:09 2026 -0600

    refactor: type the last twelve primitives that were not forced by the language
    
    "Why primitives at all?" was the right question. I had been splitting
    them into "forced" and "fine", and the second pile was doing no work.
    Splitting them properly into "forced" and "I just didn't type it" left
    twelve in the second pile, and all twelve are now typed.
    
    `baud-core` goes from 15 raw-integer sites to 8:
    
    * **`LaneMask` / `Lane`.** Six SIMD sites carried two different
      quantities as bare integers: a movemask is a *bitset over lanes* and
      `trailing_zeros()` of it is a lane *index*. `mask + i` compiles and is
      nonsense; `lane.offset_from(i)` is what the code meant. The mask can no
      longer be added to anything, and a lane index only becomes a `ByteLen`
      by being combined with the bytes already consumed.
    * **`SubParams`.** The colon/semicolon bitmask was a `u16` in two places
      and got shifted whenever a parser handed out a sub-slice. Shifting the
      wrong quantity by the wrong amount is exactly what would make
      `38:2:Pi:r:g:b` parse correctly as the first attribute of a sequence
      and wrongly as the second — silently.
    * **`ParamIdx` in the SGR loop.** That counter indexes the parameter
      array *and* realigns the mask above; as a `usize` the two could drift
      apart. It now steps by `ParamCount`, so they cannot.
    * **`RowBlock`.** Two `rows * MAX_COLS` slice computations outside the
      `Grid` helpers. Both multiply a row count by a stride, and swapped
      operands give a plausible number and a silently wrong slice.
    * **`ReportBytes.len` -> `ByteLen`, `Split.sep` -> `StreamByte`.**
    
    What remains is genuinely immovable and the audit comment now says so per
    site: three array dimensions (Rust requires a `usize` const expression;
    no newtype can go there) and five casts feeding
    `LaneMask::from_movemask`, which is the one place an intrinsic's return
    value should enter the type system. The budget is lowered 15 -> 8 so it
    cannot drift back, with a note not to raise it.
    
    **Typing the hot path is free.** These changes are inside `scan_avx2`
    and both portable scanners — the measured ingest path. Same-session A/B,
    medians of 9:
    
      cells, computed  before 1068.1 [1038.0-1085.1]  after 1073.4 [1040.7-1085.1]
      cells TUI        before  983.6 [ 957.2-1010.1]  after  983.3 [ 952.5-1012.1]
      spans, streaming before 1634.8 [1447.4-1677.0]  after 1647.0 [1064.6-1672.7]
    
    Every range overlaps. Newtypes are `repr(transparent)` and lower to the
    same instructions, so "it would cost performance" is not an argument
    against typing something here — and if it ever is, that is a measurement
    to produce rather than assume. CLAUDE.md records this.

