[33mcommit e92a2d47d27428fbfff2ff36531ed0f8ecc9544c[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 19:20:38 2026 -0600

    feat: DCS dispatch with DECRQSS, left/right margins, and OSC 8 hyperlinks
    
    The last three open rows. `docs/vt-coverage.md` now has 92 rows at
    **done** and none at `todo`, behind 306 tests in 26 files.
    
    **DCS.** All of `[[source: williams]]`'s states now exist —
    `dcs_entry`, `dcs_param`, `dcs_intermediate`, `dcs_passthrough`,
    `dcs_ignore` — so the parser is complete rather than five states of
    thirteen. DECRQSS answers for SGR, DECSTBM, DECSLRM, DECSCUSR and
    DECSCA, and answers *invalid* for everything else, since a body it made
    up would be sent straight back to it. The SGR reply always starts at `0`
    and round-trips: a report an application cannot replay is decoration.
    
    `1` is valid and `0` is invalid, and the DEC manuals say the opposite.
    `[[source: ctlseqs]]` records the errata directly — "testing a DEC VT420
    in 1996 showed that the documented code for a valid or invalid response
    to DECRQSS was reversed" — with vttest and DEC STD 070 agreeing against
    the VT420 and VT525 manuals. There is a test named for it, because a
    reader consulting the DEC manual would "fix" it backwards.
    
    Two tests I wrote asserted that a DCS payload is inert, and both were
    wrong the same way the APC test was wrong before them: a bare `ESC`
    *cancels* a control string, so `ESC [ 2 J` after one legitimately runs.
    Corrected to assert the actual guarantee — an ESC-free payload is inert —
    with the limit pinned by its own test rather than left to be discovered.
    
    **Left and right margins.** `CSI s` is genuinely ambiguous — SCOSC
    normally, DECSLRM under DECLRMM (`?69`) — so the parser is *told* the
    mode rather than guessing. `[[source: vt510-decslrm]]` requires
    `Pl < Pr`, so an inverted or empty range is rejected rather than clamped
    into something the application did not ask for. The margins bound the
    wrap (text resumes at the **left margin**, not column 0), ICH, DCH and
    DECIC/DECDC. The write path folds the right margin into the loop bound it
    already computed, so with no margins set there is no extra branch —
    `room_until` degenerates to `room_at`.
    
    **OSC 8.** The link index rides in the fourteen unused bits of
    `CellFlags`, because `PackedCell` is eight bytes *by measurement* and a
    ninth would round it to twelve; there is a test asserting the size so
    that cannot drift. The URI table is bounded at `NLINK` and evicts on
    collision, like the style table and for the reason CLAUDE.md gives: a URI
    is attacker-supplied content used as a key, and a structure keyed on that
    which grows without limit is the content-addressing failure mode. An
    empty URI *closes* a run rather than opening a link to nowhere.
    
    `replies_are_well_formed` grew to cover three families — CSI, DCS and
    OSC — and walks the whole buffer, so a reply running past its terminator
    is caught as the next one failing to start with ESC.
    
    Four more sites went through the type audit rather than around it:
    `link_len` is `[ByteLen]`, the link hash became `LinkId::bucket`
    alongside `StyleId::bucket` (taking the high bits, for the reason already
    recorded there), and `mouse_sgr: bool` became `MouseEncoding`.
    
    Measured same-session; every range overlaps, so no regression:
    
      cells, computed  before 1074.2 [1048.6-1088.0]  after 1072.4 [1017.4-1083.7]
      cells TUI        before  942.9 [ 910.5- 953.5]  after  958.2 [ 916.9-1003.0]
      spans, streaming before 1655.7 [1512.8-1688.0]  after 1650.7 [1247.7-1678.5]

