[33mcommit 85a79284a2fea7dcede7b57cb6fbc070136c3ed4[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 18:40:41 2026 -0600

    feat: OSC dispatch — titles, colour palette, and two deliberate refusals
    
    `osc_string` was `partial`: the payload was consumed to the terminator
    and thrown away, which is the "accepted, did nothing" failure
    `docs/vt-coverage.md` exists to catch. It is now captured and
    dispatched.
    
    Implemented: `OSC 0/1/2` (icon name and window title), `OSC 4` including
    the `?` query, and `OSC 104` palette reset. Replies use the same
    terminator the query arrived with, per `[[source: ctlseqs]]`: "when
    returning information, uses the same terminator used in a query."
    
    Payloads are bounded by `OSC_MAX` and **truncated rather than dropped** —
    dropping would leave the previous title showing with nothing to say why,
    and growing to fit is not available to a `no_std` core. Truncations are
    counted, not silent.
    
    Three refusals, each a decision rather than a gap:
    
    * `OSC 52` clipboard *reads* get no reply. A hostile program on the far
      end of an ssh session could otherwise read back whatever the user last
      copied. Replying with anything, empty included, tells it the feature
      works — so the refusal is silence. The variant exists in the type so
      the refusal is recorded rather than fallen into.
    * Colour *names* are not resolved. That needs X11's rgb.txt, which baud
      has no citable copy of; approximating would be inventing a protocol.
    * Querying a colour nothing overrode says nothing, because the core holds
      no built-in palette — index-to-pixels belongs to the renderer.
    
    `ESC` inside a payload got its own state. `ESC \` dispatches; anything
    else *cancels* the string per `[[source: williams]]` and begins a fresh
    sequence. Folding it into `Escape` loses the payload either way. Both
    feeds dispatch: the fast path used to scan to the terminator and discard,
    which would now mean a title set in one read silently doing nothing while
    the same bytes split across two reads worked.
    
    `XParseColor` scaling is from the top — `rgb:f/f/f` is white, not
    rgb(15,15,15) — which is the easy thing to get wrong and is tested at one
    and four digits per channel.
    
    `osc_st: bool` became `StringTerm { St, Bel }`, `osc_truncated: bool`
    became a `Stat` counter, and `Chan` gained `index()`, taking the type
    audit back from 20 to 14 rather than raising its budget.
    
    Measured same-session against the previous commit; every range overlaps,
    so no regression:
    
      cells, computed  before 1100.4 [1042.9-1114.6]  after 1056.5 [1045.8-1061.5]
      cells TUI        before  968.0 [ 935.2- 997.2]  after 1016.0 [ 982.9-1028.6]
      spans, streaming before 1692.2 [1526.5-1737.5]  after 1696.2 [1212.6-1719.6]

