[33mcommit 29dfde2181e05af829deedebf05136ae8bba9229[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 18:03:07 2026 -0600

    feat: per-cell protection, typed protocol replies, and two real bugs the properties found
    
    Follows the DECSCA/DECSED/DECSEL commit. Three things, and two of them are
    fixes to bugs that commit shipped or inherited.
    
    **Protection moves from the style to the cell.** It was a field of
    `StyleWord`, read back out of `tmpl_key` at erase time. `tmpl_key` is a
    64-slot direct-mapped cache that evicts: once an application had cycled
    through more than NSTYLE renditions -- which truecolour programs do in
    ordinary use -- the slot held somebody else and the answer was whatever
    that style happened to say. Protection was silently lost, or granted to
    text that never asked for it. It now lives in `CellFlags`, in what used
    to be `PackedCell::_pad`, where nothing can evict it. Same eight bytes.
    `protection_survives_style_eviction` fails on the previous commit.
    
    Keeping it out of the interning key also stops DECSCA halving the
    template cache: protected and unprotected text of one colour are one
    style, not two.
    
    **CPR reported a column that does not exist.** With autowrap on the
    internal cursor sits one past the last column -- the deferred-wrap
    sentinel -- and that leaked out through DSR 6 as `CSI 1 ; 201 R` on a
    200-column page. `[[source: vt510-decawm]]` puts the cursor *at* the
    right border, not beyond it. An application that saved and restored the
    cursor drifted one column, silently, only on full lines. `Term::cursor()`
    now clamps, so embedders drawing a cursor get the same fix.
    
    **Replies are typed.** `Report` mirrors `Csi`: the parse side has had a
    type since the beginning while the reply side was byte literals and a
    hand-rolled formatter at the call site. The shape is now chosen by the
    variant, so `docs/vt-coverage.md`'s "never answer a query with the wrong
    shape" is enforced by the compiler rather than by care. `Esc` does the
    same for `ESC Fe` -- `b'M'` and `b'D'` are not the names of anything.
    
    `properties.rs::ingest_is_chunk_invariant` was false as written. It
    compared `OpMode::Runs` viewports across chunkings, which is
    representation, not content, and representation is chunk-dependent by
    construction: MAXRUN is 8, so a ninth run promotes. It passed at 200
    cases and failed at 20,000 -- a test that goes red on an unlucky seed for
    a reason that is not a bug. Fixed to compare rendered content, with the
    fact pinned deterministically in
    `promotion_depends_on_chunking_in_runs_mode`.
    
    Measured, same box, same session, medians of 9 with ranges:
    
      cells, computed  HEAD 1104.2 [1089.8-1121.8]   now 1090.9 [1069.5-1096.1]
      spans, streaming HEAD 1771.0 [1162.3-1787.0]   now 1725.6 [1352.3-1745.8]
    
    Ranges overlap, so there is no regression. Getting there took two
    measured fixes, both recorded in CLAUDE.md: `CellFlags` is `u16` because
    `{u32,u16,u8,u8}` cost 4% against `{u32,u16,u16}`, and `put_ascii_run`
    branches on the flag outside the loop because threading it as a runtime
    value cost a further 5% (1049.5 vs 1127.0 with it constant).

