[33mcommit 429ad3c482357938958a87b676667700603c3ed7[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 17:04:00 2026 -0600

    feat: SGR actually applies, plus REP and DECALN
    
    SGR was the largest `parsed` gap in the codebase and docs/vt-coverage.md
    recorded it only as "partial". SgrAttr::fold handled Reset and foreground
    colour, falling through to "no change" for Set, Unset and every Bg -- so bold,
    italic, underline, reverse, blink, conceal, strike and ALL background colours
    were parsed and discarded. Support in the parser, nothing on the screen.
    
    The cause was structural: StyleWord was a bare u32 holding a 24-bit foreground
    and nothing else, so fold had nowhere to put what it parsed. Its doc comment
    claimed "24-bit colour plus attribute bits"; there were no attribute bits.
    
    StyleWord now carries foreground, background and attributes as a zeroable
    repr(C) struct, and DEFAULT is all-zero so a new_box_zeroed Storage starts in
    the default rendition rather than at an arbitrary grey. The bucket hash widens
    to 64-bit and keeps the recorded lesson: take the HIGH bits, because SGR
    colours are multiples of 0x101010 and their low bits collide.
    
    Also: the SGR parameters whose Attrs flags existed but were never set (5, 6, 8,
    9, 21, 25, 28, 29), the aixterm bright colours as palette indices 8..15, REP,
    and DECALN. REP records the last graphic character on BOTH write paths -- plain
    ASCII never reaches put_cp, so recording it only there would repeat something
    stale.
    
    DEC Special Graphics is DECLINED, not deferred silently. vt100.net publishes
    the mapping as a figure rather than text, so there is no citable table, and the
    line-drawing translation is not written from memory. The manifest records it as
    `gated`, which means no claim may rest on it; the designators are consumed
    safely and select nothing.
    
    PERFORMANCE. The redesign recovered the regression the protocol work had cost:
    streaming 1741.7 -> ~1600 -> 1756.0, ending slightly above where it started
    while the terminal now applies attributes it used to drop. TUI is 2276.0 ->
    2076.7 and that ~9% is not recovered. ghostty was untouched and moved
    1123.9 -> 1135.8, so this is the change and not drift. Both payloads are now
    clean non-overlap results against ghostty: 1.55x and 1.97x.

