[33mcommit d7d3b52a6025043f7a4b2674fa5936e7135b8210[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 16:52:37 2026 -0600

    docs: protocol roadmap, and the measured cost of correctness
    
    docs/protocol-roadmap.md recommends what to add next and what to decline. The
    ordering rule is not popularity but "what does an application break on if this
    is missing", so bracketed paste ranks above anything visual -- without it a
    pasted string containing a newline executes in the shell, which is the
    paste-jacking class -- and the alternate screen ranks first, because quitting
    vim without it loses the user's scrollback and reads as data loss.
    
    Sixel, ReGIS, kitty graphics, DECUDK, NRCS and Tektronix are recommended
    AGAINST, with reasons. Declining is a decision and belongs in the record. Note
    that baud already consumes APC and DCS payloads without executing them, which
    is the bar for safely ignoring a protocol -- and was a real bug until Tier 0.
    
    CLAUDE.md, README.md and BUILD.md now point at the coverage matrix as the
    source of truth, carry the "get the specification before writing the code"
    rule with the three times the spec overruled a confident guess, and record the
    two harness traps that manufacture false test failures here.
    
    PERFORMANCE. The protocol work cost throughput and the bill is on the record
    rather than quietly absorbed:
    
      baud, from memory      before    after
        streaming            1741.7    ~1600   (-8%)
        TUI                  2276.0    ~2120   (-7%)
    
    ghostty was untouched and moved 1123.9 -> 1138.9 over the same runs, so this
    is the change and not drift. Most of it was one avoidable mistake: two
    modes.is_set(AutoWrap) reads inside put_run's inner loop, which runs per span.
    Hoisting recovered 1540 -> 1600; the rest is work the terminal now does.
    
    The margin over ghostty is 1.42x streaming and 1.98x TUI, down from 1.55x and
    2.14x. TUI has no range overlap. Streaming is stated as a MEDIAN result, not a
    range result: baud is the noisiest core here and its minimum dips into
    ghostty's range in one of two runs, so claiming non-overlap on streaming would
    be overstating it.

