[33mcommit 4090c8990aff6ef84494414c19aae8f9d0ebad22[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 16:48:28 2026 -0600

    feat: DECSET/DECRST for the modes baud actually implements
    
    DECSET/DECRST were `parsed` -- recognised and dropped. Now DECOM, DECAWM and
    DECTCEM act, and nothing else is recorded: mouse reporting, bracketed paste and
    the alternate screen stay inert because they are input-side or need a second
    screen buffer, and a bit that is set and never read is the same "accepted, did
    nothing" failure.
    
    Semantics are from the VT510 programmer reference, fetched and hash-pinned
    rather than recalled:
    
    - DECOM: "the home cursor position is at the upper-left corner of the screen,
      within the margins. The starting point for line numbers depends on the
      current top margin setting. The cursor cannot move outside of the margins."
      So CUP and VPA are relative to the top margin, and *every* movement is
      confined -- my first attempt confined only absolute addressing, and the test
      written from that sentence caught it.
    - DECAWM: whether received characters wrap at the right border.
    
    A SOURCE CONFLICT, recorded rather than smoothed over. The VT510 manual gives
    DECAWM's default as "No autowrap"; ctlseqs documents xterm, where it is on, and
    every modern terminal wraps. baud follows xterm, because an application
    emitting a long line expects it to wrap and the DEC default would break
    essentially all of them. The stricter reading is the one baud does not
    implement, and docs/vt-coverage.md says so.
    
    Two bugs the tests found in my own implementation:
    
    - put_cp was patched for DECAWM and put_run was not, so bulk text -- which is
      almost all text -- still wrapped.
    - With autowrap off the cursor ended one past the last column. That position is
      the "wrap is pending" sentinel; with no pending wrap it is not reachable, and
      the cursor belongs on the last cell.
    
    10 tests in vt_modes.rs.

