[33mcommit 9f135860ebcde42114428088e1416b0b0eb6e167[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 16:43:57 2026 -0600

    feat: a reply channel, and the queries that need it
    
    docs/vt-coverage.md called this the largest structural gap, bigger than any
    operation count, and it was right: a terminal is not write-only. DA, DSR and
    DECRQM are questions, and an application that asks one and gets nothing back
    hangs rather than degrading.
    
    Storage.reply is a 256-byte buffer the core fills and the caller drains with
    Term::reply() / Term::clear_reply(). It mirrors the input side deliberately --
    the core is no_std with no I/O and cannot own a PTY, so the same shape that
    works for read_slot works here. Overflow increments reply_overflows rather
    than dropping answers silently, and a test floods it to prove the counter
    moves.
    
    Response formats are from ctlseqs, not memory: DSR 5 -> `CSI 0 n`,
    DSR 6 -> `CSI r ; c R`, and the Primary DA identities are the list under
    `CSI Ps c`.
    
    Two decisions where the wrong answer is worse than none:
    
    - DA answers `CSI ? 6 c`, VT102. That is what baud is: DECSTBM from the VT100,
      IL/DL from the VT102, and no sixel, ReGIS, UDKs, selective erase or
      132-column mode. Over-claiming makes applications send sequences baud drops;
      under-claiming only makes them use less.
    - An unsupported DSR gets no reply. Answering with the wrong report shape is
      worse than silence, because the application parses whatever arrives as the
      report it asked for. `CSI ? 6 n` is a different namespace and is not
      answered as if it were the ANSI one.
    
    The audit caught the one real design slip: emit_num took a `usize`, which is
    the "two quantities confused" shape the newtypes exist to prevent, and a
    coordinate report is exactly where an off-by-one stays invisible until an
    application draws in the wrong place. It takes a OneBased now, with
    Row::one_based/Col::one_based as the typed conversion, and a test round-trips
    a CPR back through CUP so the two cannot disagree on 0- vs 1-basing.
    
    9 tests in vt_replies.rs.

