    feat: complete the C0 controls
    
    VT and FF were dropped, so a stream containing either lost its line break
    entirely. Both are an index -- a terminal does not eject a page -- and they are
    asserted equal to ESC D, including scrolling at the region bottom.
    
    BEL was dropped too. There is no UI here to ring one, so it is counted and
    exposed: a core that silently discards BEL leaves an embedder no way to
    implement one, which is the same "accepted, did nothing, no way to find out"
    failure the coverage matrix calls `parsed`.
    
    NUL was already discarded, by falling through rather than by decision. It has
    a test now, and so does the general rule that an unhandled C0 byte is
    discarded and never printed -- a terminal that prints an unknown control
    renders mojibake into the user's screen.
    
