[33mcommit fa5e3c3c1aeeb6818058ca28ac7eba28b47d2eb5[m
Author: Ido Samuelson <i-am-logger@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Wed Aug 26 16:12:54 2026 -0600

    feat: cursor positioning and a real tab stop table
    
    Thirteen Tier-1 operations, none of which existed.
    
    Cursor positioning: CNL, CPL, CHA, HPA, VPA, HPR, VPR, SCOSC, SCORC. Each has
    a default parameter and a clamping rule and both are where these usually go
    wrong, so the tests pin them: omitted is 1, an explicit 0 is also 1, and every
    move clamps to the screen rather than wrapping. CHA and HPA are one operation
    under two names and are asserted to agree; VPR keeps the column where CNL does
    not, which is the pair most often conflated.
    
    Tab stops are one feature under five names, and none of them worked. HT used
    fixed every-eight arithmetic against no table at all, so HTS could not set a
    stop, TBC could not clear one, and CHT/CBT did not exist. Storage.tabs is now
    one flag per column, defaulted every eight and restored by RIS.
    
    TBC takes the two values xterm implements, 0 and 3. Anything else is inert
    rather than aliased onto 0 -- silently treating an unknown parameter as "clear
    at cursor" is how a terminal ends up clearing stops an application asked it to
    keep.
    
    CHT/CBT counts clamp to the column count. There cannot be more stops than
    columns, and without the clamp `CSI 65535 I` spins 65535 times once the cursor
    is already at the margin: bounded, since Count is u16, but work a hostile
    stream should not be able to ask for.
    
    24 new tests across vt_cursor.rs and vt_tabs.rs. docs/vt-coverage.md moves 13
    rows to done.
    
    Not claimed: whether this closes the tab-stop failures the differential test
    names. That needs a differential run against an alacritty checkout, which this
    machine does not have, so the matrix records it as unverified rather than
    assuming the fix landed.

